---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import fallFestivalPhoto from '../../assets/communities/goddard/goddard-fall-festival-movie-in-the-park-city-of-goddard.jpg';
import ferrisWheelPhoto from '../../assets/communities/goddard/goddard-fall-festival-ferris-wheel-city-of-goddard.jpg';
import fireworksPhoto from '../../assets/communities/goddard/goddard-fall-festival-fireworks-city-of-goddard.jpg';
import tanganyikaPhoto from '../../assets/communities/goddard/goddard-tanganyika-wildlife-park-kansastourism-2016 Ryan Donnell.jpg';
import linearParkPhoto from '../../assets/communities/goddard/goddard-splash-pad-with-kids-city-of-goddard.jpg';
import mainStreetPhoto from '../../assets/communities/goddard/goddard-street-aerial-2-city-of-goddard.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Goddard, Kansas Community Guide | Charity Menefee"
  description="A practical introduction to Goddard, Kansas, including its location west of Wichita, older Main Street core, residential growth, and property considerations."
  pageClass="page-interior page-goddard"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Community guide · Goddard"
    title="Small-town roots, with growth all around."
    intro="Goddard is its own city immediately west of Wichita, where an older community centered around Main Street meets substantial newer residential growth."
    image={fallFestivalPhoto}
    imageAlt="A crowd seated on blankets and lawn chairs watching an outdoor movie screen at dusk during the Goddard Fall Festival"
    variant="community"
    imagePosition="center 60%"
    imagePositionMobile="center 55%"
    photoCredit="© City of Goddard"
  />

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="goddard-overview-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Getting oriented</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-overview-title">An independent city on the west side of the metro.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Goddard is an incorporated city in western Sedgwick County, immediately west of Wichita. US-54/400, commonly called Kellogg, provides a direct east-west connection between the two cities.</p>
        <p>Goddard combines an established small-town core with considerable newer growth around it. New neighborhoods continue to expand the community, while the city's sports and recreation district, including tournament fields and Blast Off Bay indoor water park, has added amenities not typically associated with a city of Goddard's size. Wichita remains nearby, particularly for those who regularly travel to the city's west side.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="goddard-housing-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Housing in a growing city</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-housing-title">New residential development is changing the city's footprint.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Goddard includes older established housing as well as newer residential development. City records identify Arbor Creek South and Rustic Creek among the additions contributing to that changing footprint.</p>
        <p>Those names illustrate where growth has occurred, but they don't confirm current construction or availability. The age and type of development can affect the lot, surrounding infrastructure, included improvements, and any HOA or special-assessment obligations tied to a property.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="photo-banner section-sage" aria-labelledby="goddard-character-title">
    <div class="photo-banner-media">
      <Picture
        src={mainStreetPhoto}
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
        widths={[960, 1440, 1920, 2600]}
        sizes="100vw"
        alt="An aerial view of Main Street in Goddard, with older storefronts in the foreground and newer rooftops spreading toward the horizon"
      />
      <p class="photo-credit">© City of Goddard</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell photo-banner-copy" data-reveal="up">
      <p class="eyebrow">Local character and change</p>
      <h2 id="goddard-character-title">Main Street is still the older side of a growing city.</h2>
      <p>Goddard was incorporated in 1910, and Main Street historically served as the city's primary business area. That older physical core, visible here, remains an important point of contrast with the newer residential development spreading toward the edges of town.</p>
      <p>Along the US-54 corridor, the Genesis Sports Complex represents a newer side of Goddard's growth. Its tournament and recreation facilities extend that story beyond housing without replacing the city's older center.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="goddard-festival-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">A yearly tradition</p>
          <h2 id="goddard-festival-title">Main Street hosts the Fall Festival.</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">Every October the festival takes over Main Street, a tradition since the 1960s. It's the clearest annual example of Main Street still working as the city's gathering place, which is worth knowing if you're weighing a home in the older part of town against one further out.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card-grid reveal-stagger">
        <figure class="feature-card" data-reveal="left-scale">
          <div class="feature-card-media">
            <Picture
              src={ferrisWheelPhoto}
              formats={['avif', 'webp']}
              widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
              sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw"
              alt="An illuminated Ferris wheel and carnival rides against the night sky at the Goddard Fall Festival"
            />
            <p class="photo-credit">© City of Goddard</p>
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Parade and carnival</strong>
            <p>The parade runs up Main Street from 23rd to 4th, and the surrounding blocks fill with carnival rides, vendor booths, and food trucks near Linear Park.</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="feature-card" data-reveal="right-scale">
          <div class="feature-card-media">
            <Picture
              src={fireworksPhoto}
              formats={['avif', 'webp']}
              widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
              sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 50vw, 100vw"
              alt="Fireworks bursting above the stage and crowd at the Goddard Fall Festival"
            />
            <p class="photo-credit">© City of Goddard</p>
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Through the weekend</strong>
            <p>An outdoor movie screening, contests, and tournaments fill out the rest of the schedule, and the festival runs into the evening with live entertainment and fireworks.</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="photo-story section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="goddard-tanganyika-title">
    <div class="shell photo-story-grid photo-story-reverse tanganyika-grid">
      <div class="photo-story-copy" data-reveal="right">
        <p class="eyebrow">A local attraction</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-tanganyika-title">Tanganyika Wildlife Park is here, not just nearby.</h2>
        <p>Tanganyika Wildlife Park sits on South Hawkins Lane, inside Goddard. It grew out of a breeding facility the Fouts family started in 1985 and opened to the public in 2008. Today it holds more than 40 exhibits and over 400 animals, and it's accredited by the Zoological Association of America.</p>
        <p>The park is built around hands-on encounters rather than viewing from a distance, including feeding stations and a walkthrough kangaroo area. It draws visitors from well outside Sedgwick County, and it's one of the things people most often associate with Goddard.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-story-main photo-story-tanganyika" data-reveal="left">
        <Picture
          src={tanganyikaPhoto}
          formats={['avif', 'webp']}
          widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
          sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 62vw, 100vw"
          alt="A Tanganyika Wildlife Park staff member and a visitor crouching in the grass beside a serval"
        />
        <p class="photo-credit">© 2016 Ryan Donnell</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="photo-story section-space section-sage" aria-labelledby="goddard-linear-park-title">
    <div class="shell photo-story-grid">
      <div class="photo-story-copy" data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everyday recreation</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-linear-park-title">Goddard Linear Park follows an old rail corridor.</h2>
        <p>Linear Park opened in 2009 along the route of a former railroad line just off Main Street. It includes a splash pad, a playground with sensory and inclusive features, a picnic shelter, restrooms, and a community storm shelter. The Cecile Kellenbarger Memorial Covered Bridge, dedicated in 2012, recognizes the effort behind converting the corridor.</p>
        <p>The Prairie Sunset Trail runs through the park on its way east toward Wichita and west toward Garden Plain, a rail-banked path of roughly fifteen miles used for walking, running, and biking. For a property near the older part of the city, that trail is worth checking on a map.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-story-main" data-reveal="right">
        <Picture
          src={linearParkPhoto}
          formats={['avif', 'webp']}
          widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280, 1600]}
          sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 62vw, 100vw"
          alt="Water features running at the Goddard Linear Park splash pad, with a shade canopy and playground beyond"
        />
        <p class="photo-credit">© City of Goddard</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="goddard-practical-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical things to consider</p>
        <h2 id="goddard-practical-title">The development around a home can matter as much as its age.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Start by confirming whether a property is inside Goddard city limits and how it connects to US-54/400 and the roads you expect to use. Then compare the home's age, lot characteristics, utilities, maintenance needs, and development setting.</p>
        <p>For newer construction, verify what's included with the home and lot, which restrictions apply, and whether assessments, utility arrangements, or HOA obligations are connected to that address.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="goddard-search-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Useful questions</p>
          <h2 id="goddard-search-title">What should you verify when looking in Goddard?</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">The answers can vary between an established property and a home in a newer or still-developing area.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="question-grid reveal-stagger">
        <li data-reveal="up">Is this property in an established part of Goddard or a newer development?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">For new construction, what's included with the home and lot, and are HOA requirements or special assessments tied to the property?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">How does the location connect to US-54/400 and the roads you'd actually use?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Which details about the home's age, lot, utilities, maintenance, or restrictions need verification?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">If the surrounding area is still developing, which improvements or future phases should be reviewed?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="shell next-community" aria-label="Community pages">
    <span>Keep exploring</span>
    <a href="/communities/">All communities <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></a>
  </nav>
  <CallToAction
    title="Have questions about a property in Goddard?"
    copy="If you're comparing communities or have questions about a specific property, tell me what you're considering. I’ll help you sort through the location and property details that matter."
  />
</BaseLayout>
